+## Staged activation
+
+Transfer and activation can be separated when a reboot is only safe in a later
+maintenance window. `stage` validates policy, transfers the image into the
+inactive slot, and stops after the device has verified the image digest. No
+candidate slot is selected and the device keeps running its confirmed firmware.
+
+```sh
+fwctl --device sensor-0042 stage sensor-node-1.2.0.fwpkg
+fwctl staged
+fwctl --device sensor-0042 activate
+```
+
+Each staged transfer is journaled locally, one record per device, and `activate`
+completes it from that record alone: it reconnects, checks that the device still
+matches the record, verifies the digest again, selects the candidate slot,
+reboots, health-checks, and confirms. The record is consumed whatever the
+outcome. A device that no longer matches its record fails with
+`staged_update_lost` before any boot state changes, and a device without a record
+fails with `nothing_staged`.
+
 Every command accepts `--json`; progress remains on standard error so standard
 output is a single machine-readable record. `--quiet` suppresses successful human
 output, while `--verbose` reports configuration and connection detail.
 
